      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can reproduce this issue when switching from a small avatar to a normal-height avatar that uses the Unity Cloth component.\n\n**Reproduction steps:**\n\n1. Switch to a small avatar.\n\n2. Switch to a normal-height avatar with a Cloth-based skirt.\n\n3. The skirt becomes significantly shorter than its intended length.\n\n**Expected behavior:**\n\nThe Cloth mesh should maintain its correct dimensions regardless of the previously used avatar.\n\n**Actual behavior:**\n\nThe Cloth mesh appears to inherit scaling information from the previously used avatar, causing the skirt to shrink.\n\n**Possible regression:**\n\nSimilar Cloth scaling issues were previously fixed in VRChat 2023.3.2 and 2023.4.2. A related Unity 2022 Open Beta report was also marked Complete in April 2024.\n\nThis may be a regression of those previous fixes, potentially related to the Unity 6 upgrade.\n\nI've attached comparison screenshots showing the incorrect and correct skirt lengths.\n\nCould the developers investigate whether the previous Cloth scaling fixes are still functioning correctly?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
