      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would also like to point out a potentially related regression involving Unity Cloth scaling.\n\nIn addition to the avatar-switching issue reported here, there is another reproducible issue where changing the current avatar's height using VRChat's built-in Avatar Height adjustment causes the Cloth mesh to scale incorrectly.\n\nImportantly, this second issue occurs without switching avatars.\n\nThe existing report for that issue is here:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/cloth-applied-mesh-does-not-scale-when-avatar-scale-is-changed\n\nA related Cloth scaling issue was previously marked as fixed in the Unity 2022 Open Beta:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/cloth-applied-mesh-does-not-scale-when-avatar-scale-is-changed\n\nSince both issues involve incorrect Cloth scaling, I wonder whether they could share a common problem with Cloth initialization or scale handling after the Unity 6 migration.\n\nThe root cause is not confirmed, but I hope these reports can be investigated together.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
